[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "Route '/sign-up'. Exposes exactly: one text input with label 'Username' (id/name username), one text input with label 'Email' (id/name email), one type=password input labelled 'Password' (id/name password), one type=password input labelled 'Confirm password' (id/name confirmPassword), one initially unchecked checkbox named/labelled 'Agree to the terms' (id/name agreeToTerms), and one always-actionable submit button whose text is 'Create account' (disabled only while an in-flight request is pending). Password values must never be rendered as text and must not appear in any visible/echoed node. On submit, POST the five values to /api/auth/register via authApi.registerAccount. On failure: stay on /sign-up, render every returned field error simultaneously in dedicated elements (data-testid and aria-describedby targets username-error, email-error, password-error, confirm-password-error, terms-error; role=alert), keep the username and email inputs unchanged, and never add an account. Message text mapping is server-owned: username -> 'Username already exists' | 'Username format is invalid', email -> 'Email format is invalid', password -> 'Password requirements are not satisfied', confirmPassword -> mismatch message, terms -> 'Agree to terms is required'. On success: the created account already has a verified email, so navigate to '/sign-in' (no email-verification page exists in this product) and do not create a duplicate. Layout/labels/id/error-slot contract only in DESIGN; validation logic, error retention and success handling are TDD work.",
