[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "req_id": "REQ-1-1-1",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "type": "FUNC",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "name": "auth_service (registration validation, account creation, session lifecycle)",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "file_path": "backend/src/services/auth_service.js",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "first_line": 1,
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "responsibility": "Own the auth business rules: input validation with a shared message catalog, duplicate detection, password hashing, account creation with verified email, credential verification and session persistence.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "Exports SESSION_COOKIE, FIELD_MESSAGES ('Username already exists', 'Username format is invalid', 'Email format is invalid', 'Password requirements are not satisfied', 'Agree to terms is required', mismatch message), validateUsername/validateEmail/validatePassword, validateRegistration(payload), registerAccount(payload), signIn(payload), getSessionUser(req), signOut(req,res). Validation rules (enforced by TDD): username trimmed, 1-39 chars of lowercase ASCII letters/digits with single hyphens and no leading/trailing hyphen; email trimmed of outer whitespace, <=254 chars, exactly one '@', at least one dot and non-empty domain labels after '@'; password 12-128 chars, no whitespace, at least one uppercase, one lowercase, one digit and one non-alphanumeric special character; confirmPassword must equal password; agreeToTerms must be true; username/email uniqueness checked against accounts.username_key/email_key. validateRegistration collects every failing field at once (no early return) so the UI can show username+email+password+terms messages for one submission. registerAccount hashes the password, inserts the account with email_verified = 1 and lowercase-trimmed keys, then creates the session record/cookie; it returns { ok: true, user } | { ok: false, errors } and must never persist on failure. signIn looks up by case-insensitive email, verifies the hash and creates the session. getSessionUser resolves { id, username, email, emailVerified } from the cookie via sessions -> accounts, else null.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "inputs": "Raw registration/sign-in payloads; Express req/res for cookie access; DB helpers from backend/src/database/db_runtime.js.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "outputs": "{ ok, user } | { ok, errors } results; session rows/cookies; public SessionUser shapes without password material.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "callers": [
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]         "REQ-1-1-1-API-AUTH-ROUTES"
