[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "type": "DB",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "name": "accounts + sessions schema and deterministic seed",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "file_path": "backend/src/database/init_db.js",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "first_line": 1,
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "responsibility": "Persist sign-in-capable accounts with verified-email status plus durable session records, and guarantee the baseline account required by the scenarios exists after normal startup.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "init_db.js adds, idempotently inside initializeDatabase, CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS accounts (id PK AUTOINCREMENT, username, username_key, email, email_key, password_hash, email_verified INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1, created_at) with UNIQUE indexes on username_key and email_key (case-insensitive lookup via *_key and/or COLLATE NOCASE), and CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (token PK, account_id REFERENCES accounts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, created_at). seed_db.js (invoked by the normal seed/bootstrap path, never by test-only setup) must ensure, deterministically and idempotently (INSERT OR IGNORE / upsert on the unique keys, reuse of the service password-hash helper), the baseline account used by the account-access scenarios: username `alice-dev`, email `alice.dev@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`, email_verified = 1, able to sign in through the normal path. Seed remains ordinary product state — no test-only DSL, no hardcoded fallback arrays in the UI, and only the records named by the requirement are seeded (registration inputs typed during a scenario must never be pre-inserted).",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "inputs": "application startup / npm run db:seed via backend/src/database/seed_db.js; schema migration step in initializeDatabase.",
[2026-09-26T16:09:50.483+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "outputs": "accounts and sessions tables available through db_runtime helpers; one seeded verified baseline account.",
